---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const domainColor = '#f59e0b'; // Amber for Medical Review
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Medical Review Agent — Medivora"
  description="Architecture and capabilities of the Medivora Medical Review Agent for automating seriousness, expectedness, and causality assessments."
>
  <article class="agent-detail-page">
    
    <!-- ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <header class="agent-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="breadcrumb">
          <a href="/agents">← Back to Agents</a>
        </div>
        
        <div class="hero-meta">
          <span class="domain-tag" style={`--dc: ${domainColor}`}>Pharmacovigilance</span>
          <span class="phase-tag">Phase 3 · Review</span>
          <span class="date-tag">Last reviewed: Jun 2025</span>
        </div>
        
        <h1 class="agent-title">Medical Review Copilot</h1>
        <p class="agent-tagline">AI reasoning assistant for the human QPPV or medical reviewer.</p>

        <div class="agent-hero-pattern" style="--agent-accent: rgba(245,158,11,0.12)"></div>
        
        <div class="reading-meta">
          <span class="reading-meta-item">📖 14 min read</span>
          <span class="reading-meta-item">📅 Updated 2025-06-02</span>
          <button class="btn-print" onclick="window.print()">🖨 Save as PDF</button>
        </div>

        <nav class="pipeline-indicator" aria-label="ICSR Pipeline Position">
          <a href="/agents/intake-triage" class="pipeline-step">Intake</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/meddra-coding" class="pipeline-step">Coding</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/medical-review" class="pipeline-step active">Review</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/aggregate-reporting" class="pipeline-step">Reporting</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/literature-monitoring" class="pipeline-step">Literature</a>
          <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
          <a href="/agents/regulatory-intelligence" class="pipeline-step">RegIntel</a>
        </nav>

        <div class="agent-metrics">
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">0<sup>[1]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">Black-box decisions</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">100%<sup>[2]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">QPPV sign-off rate</span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric-box">
            <span class="mb-val">60%<sup>[3]</sup></span>
            <span class="mb-lbl">Reduction in review cycle time</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top:1.5rem; padding-top:1rem; border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06);">
          <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.62rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.4); margin-bottom:0.6rem;">References & Sources</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[1] EU GVP Module VI — Requirement for transparent reasoning traces <span class="" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Design Principle)</span></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[2] Directive 2001/83/EC, Article 104 <span class="" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Regulatory Requirement)</span></p>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin:0.2rem 0;">[3] Gartner, 'Hype Cycle for Life Science R&D', 2024 <span class="risk-med" style="font-size:0.6rem;">(Projected)</span></p>
        </div>

        <div class="reviewed-by-band">
          <div class="rb-icon">✓</div>
          <div class="rb-text">
            Content reviewed by <strong>Kritnandan</strong>, B.Tech BSBE (IIT Kanpur) | Last review: Jun 2025 | Review cadence: Quarterly
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ── THE PROBLEM ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-light problem-section">
      <div class="wrap content-grid">
        <div class="cg-main">
          <h2>The Cognitive Load on Physicians</h2>
          <p class="lead-text">
            Medical review is the most expensive and critical step in PV. Highly trained physicians spend hours comparing coded adverse events against hundreds of pages of Reference Safety Information (RSI) or Investigator Brochures (IB) to determine expectedness and causality.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Medivora Medical Review Agent acts as a co-pilot for safety physicians. It instantly cross-references the coded case against the current, approved product label, drafts a causality assessment with clinical rationale, and highlights discrepancies for the human reviewer to make the final call.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="cg-side info-panel">
          <h4>Agent Profile</h4>
          <dl class="agent-specs">
            <dt>Data Inputs</dt>
            <dd>Fully coded ICSRs, CCDS, SmPC, USPI, Investigator Brochures.</dd>
            <dt>Core AI Models</dt>
            <dd>Clinical-reasoning LLMs integrated with strict Rule Engines.</dd>
            <dt>Key Outputs</dt>
            <dd>Seriousness criteria, Expectedness flags (Listed/Unlisted), Causality narrative draft.</dd>
            <dt>Standards</dt>
            <dd>ICH E2A (Expectedness), CIOMS guidelines.</dd>
          </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── ARCHITECTURE ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark arch-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Agent Architecture &amp; Workflow</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Because medical assessment directly triggers regulatory reporting (e.g., a SUSAR), this agent utilizes a highly constrained architecture. Expectedness is driven by a deterministic rule engine querying the RSI, while causality narratives are drafted by the LLM for human approval.
        </p>
        
        <div class="diagram-container">
          <pre class="mermaid">
flowchart LR
    classDef external fill:#1a1a1a,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px,color:#888
    classDef input fill:#112a22,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef agent fill:#0a192f,stroke:#64ffda,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef db fill:#2d1b2e,stroke:#e05c8a,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef hitl fill:#3a2a00,stroke:#e8a838,stroke-width:1px,color:#fff
    classDef output fill:#112a22,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px,color:#fff

    subgraph "Case Data"
        Case["Coded Case (AEs, Drugs)"]:::external
    end

    subgraph "Assessment Layer"
        direction TB
        Expectedness["Expectedness Engine<br>(Deterministic)"]:::input
        Causality(["Causality Reasoning Agent<br>(LLM)"]):::agent
        RSIDB[("Label / RSI / CCDS<br>Database")]:::db
    end

    subgraph "Human Review & Action"
        direction TB
        Draft["Assessment Draft & Narrative"]:::agent
        Physician["Safety Physician<br>(Final Sign-off)"]:::hitl
        ReportDB["Reporting Engine (SUSAR/ICSR)"]:::output
    end

    Case --> Expectedness
    Case --> Causality
    
    RSIDB -- "Listed Terms" --> Expectedness
    RSIDB -- "Known MOA" --> Causality

    Expectedness --> Draft
    Causality --> Draft

    Draft --> Physician
    Physician -- "Approves / Edits" --> ReportDB

    linkStyle default stroke:#444,stroke-width:2px;
          </pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── CORE CAPABILITIES ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-light caps-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="section-title-dark">Core Capabilities</h2>
        <div class="caps-grid">
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">1</div>
            <h3>Deterministic Expectedness</h3>
            <p>Maps the MedDRA PT exactly against the approved product label for the specific market. Never hallucinates whether an event is "listed" or "unlisted", relying on strict database querying.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">2</div>
            <h3>Automated Causality Drafting</h3>
            <p>Generates a draft clinical narrative evaluating temporal relationship, de-challenge/re-challenge results, and alternative etiologies (e.g., patient's medical history of hypertension) to propose a causality outcome.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">3</div>
            <h3>Seriousness Upgrading</h3>
            <p>Detects if the reporter missed a seriousness criterion (e.g., the narrative mentions "hospitalized overnight" but the Seriousness flag was left unchecked) and prompts the human reviewer to upgrade the case.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="cap-card">
            <div class="cap-icon">4</div>
            <h3>Regulatory Reporting Router</h3>
            <p>If an event is deemed Serious, Unlisted, and Related, the agent immediately flags the case as a potential SUSAR/15-day report and alerts the submissions team.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  
    <!-- ── UNDER THE HOOD ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark under-hood-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Under the Hood</span>
        <h2>Architectural Deep Dive</h2>
        
        <div class="uh-grid">
          <div class="uh-col">
            <h3>Algorithmic Causality Assessment</h3>
            <p>The Medical Review agent does not rely on "gut feeling" LLM responses. It systematically walks through validated causality frameworks (like the Naranjo algorithm or WHO-UMC criteria) and outputs a scored reasoning trace.</p>
            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
              <div class="code-header"><span class="code-dot r"></span><span class="code-dot y"></span><span class="code-dot g"></span><span class="code-title">naranjo_evaluator.json</span></div>
              <pre is:raw><code>{
  "tool": "evaluate_causality",
  "parameters": {
    "temporal_relationship": {
      "assessment": "Plausible time to onset (2 days)",
      "score": 1
    },
    "dechallenge": {
      "assessment": "Event abated after drug withdrawn",
      "score": 1
    },
    "rechallenge": {
      "assessment": "No rechallenge performed",
      "score": 0
    },
    "alternative_causes": {
      "assessment": "Patient has underlying hypertension",
      "score": -1
    },
    "total_score": 1,
    "final_determination": "Possible"
  }
}</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          
          <div class="uh-col">
            <h3>Safety Narrative Generation</h3>
            <p>The agent drafts the required medical narrative by synthesizing the structured data into a chronological, regulator-ready text block.</p>
            <div class="code-block-wrapper">
              <div class="code-header"><span class="code-dot r"></span><span class="code-dot y"></span><span class="code-dot g"></span><span class="code-title">system_prompt.txt</span></div>
              <pre is:raw><code>You are drafting an ICSR Safety Narrative.

STRUCTURE REQUIRED:
1. Patient Demographics (Age, Sex, Medical History)
2. Suspect Drugs (Dose, Route, Dates of Therapy)
3. Concomitant Medications
4. Event Description (Chronological timeline of AEs)
5. Action Taken with Drug & Outcome
6. Company Causality Assessment

TONE: Objective, clinical, and passive. Do not use emotive language. Do not state facts not present in the source data.</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guardrails-box">
          <h3>Guardrails & Failure Modes</h3>
          <ul class="guardrail-list">
            <li><strong>Complex Co-morbidities:</strong> In cases with multiple interacting concomitant medications and a complex medical history, the agent's causality scoring becomes less reliable. High-complexity cases bypass autonomous review.</li>
            <li><strong>Hallucinated Test Results:</strong> LLMs can occasionally hallucinate normal ranges for lab values if not explicitly provided. The prompt strictly enforces that lab values must be copied verbatim from source docs.</li>
            <li><strong>Strict Regulatory Boundaries:</strong> The agent acts as an *assistant*. In the EU, a Qualified Person for Pharmacovigilance (QPPV) or designated medical reviewer must legally sign off on the assessment. The agent *recommends*, the human *approves*.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  
    <!-- ── SAMPLE DEMO ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark" id="sample-demo">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Interactive Demo</span>
        <h2>See It in Action</h2>
        <h3>Sample Case Walkthrough</h3>
        <span class="synthetic-watermark">Synthetic Data — Illustrative Only</span>
        <div class="sample-demo">
          <div class="demo-panel">
            <div class="demo-panel-header">Input</div>
            <div class="demo-panel-body"><pre is:raw style="white-space:pre-wrap; margin:0; font-size:0.8rem; color:#a8b2d1;">Case #2024-001: 67F, Drug-X 200mg PO daily x14d for RA.\nAE: Hepatotoxicity, ALT 5x ULN.\nAction: Drug withdrawn. Outcome: Recovering.\nConcomitant: Methotrexate 15mg/week, Folic Acid 5mg/week.</pre></div>
          </div>
          <div class="demo-panel">
            <div class="demo-panel-header">Agent Output</div>
            <div class="demo-panel-body"><pre is:raw style="white-space:pre-wrap; margin:0; font-size:0.8rem; color:#a8b2d1;">{\n  "naranjo_score": {\n    "temporal_relationship": "+1",\n    "dechallenge": "+1 (Drug withdrawn, recovering)",\n    "rechallenge": "0 (Not performed)",\n    "alternative_causes": "-1 (Methotrexate is hepatotoxic)",\n    "total": 1\n  },\n  "assessment": "Possible",\n  "narrative_draft": "A 67-year-old female patient developed hepatotoxicity (ALT elevated to 5x ULN) approximately 14 days after initiating Drug-X 200mg orally daily for rheumatoid arthritis..."\n}</pre></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── RISK & COMPLIANCE ────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark" id="risk-compliance" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.1);">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Risk & Compliance</span>
        <h2>Failure Modes, Validation & Integration</h2>
        
        <h3>Risk & Failure Mode Matrix</h3>
        <table class="risk-matrix">
          <thead><tr>
            <th>Failure Mode</th><th>Severity</th><th>Likelihood</th><th>Mitigation</th><th>Residual Risk</th>
          </tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Hallucinated lab values</td><td class="risk-high">Critical</td><td class="risk-med">Medium</td><td>Strict source-citation enforcement</td><td class="risk-low">Low</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Incorrect causality assessment</td><td class="risk-high">High</td><td class="risk-med">Medium</td><td>Naranjo algorithm + QPPV sign-off</td><td class="risk-low">Low</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Missed concomitant medication</td><td class="risk-med">Medium</td><td class="risk-high">High</td><td>Cross-reference with full narrative</td><td class="risk-med">Medium</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Narrative tone too informal</td><td class="risk-low">Low</td><td class="risk-low">Low</td><td>Medical writing style prompt + post-check</td><td class="risk-low">Negligible</td></tr>
          </tbody></table>
        
        <h3>Validation & Qualification</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.7); margin-bottom:1rem;">This agent is classified under GAMP 5 as a <strong>Category 5</strong> (Custom/Configurable) system requiring full CSV/CSA qualification.</p>
        <div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <span class="gamp-badge">GAMP 5 — Category 5</span>
          <span class="gamp-badge">21 CFR Part 11 Compliant</span>
          <span class="gamp-badge">EU Annex 11 Ready</span>
        </div>
        
        <h3>Integration Points</h3>
        <div class="integration-grid">
          <div class="integration-chip"><div><div>Safety Database</div><div class="ic-type">Primary</div></div></div>
          <div class="integration-chip"><div><div>FDA ESG</div><div class="ic-type">Submission</div></div></div>
          <div class="integration-chip"><div><div>EudraVigilance</div><div class="ic-type">Submission</div></div></div>
          <div class="integration-chip"><div><div>PMDA Gateway</div><div class="ic-type">Submission</div></div></div>
        </div>
        
        <h3>Implementation Timeline</h3>
        <div class="impl-timeline">
          <div class="impl-phase phase-active">
            <div class="impl-phase-num">Phase 1</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-name">Pilot</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-dur">4–6 weeks</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-desc">Deploy on a single product with limited case volume. Validate extraction accuracy and HITL workflows.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="impl-phase">
            <div class="impl-phase-num">Phase 2</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-name">UAT & Validation</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-dur">6–8 weeks</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-desc">Formal IQ/OQ/PQ testing. GAMP 5 documentation. CSV/CSA qualification. 21 CFR Part 11 compliance review.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="impl-phase">
            <div class="impl-phase-num">Phase 3</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-name">Production</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-dur">Ongoing</div>
            <div class="impl-phase-desc">Full deployment across product portfolio. Continuous monitoring, model retraining, and quarterly validation reviews.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── VENDOR LANDSCAPE ─────────────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark" id="vendor-landscape" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.1);">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Market Context</span>
        <h2>Vendor Landscape</h2>
        <h3>Vendor Landscape</h3>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.6); margin-bottom:1rem;">The following vendors offer capabilities in this agent category. This comparison is vendor-neutral and does not constitute an endorsement.</p>
        <table class="vendor-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Vendor / Platform</th><th>Capability</th><th>Market Segment</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Oracle Argus Safety</td><td>Integrated medical review workflow</td><td>Enterprise</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Veeva Vault Safety</td><td>Configurable review workflows</td><td>Enterprise</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Saama Technologies</td><td>AI-powered clinical data review</td><td>Mid-to-Large</td></tr>
          </tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── RESOURCES & NEXT STEPS ───────────────────────────── -->
    <section class="section-dark" id="resources" style="border-top: 1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.1);">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">Resources</span>
        <h2>Related Reading & Next Steps</h2>
        
        <div class="related-studies">
          <h3>Related Case Studies</h3>
          <div class="study-card-grid">
            <a href="/case-studies/hallucination-risk" class="study-link-card">
              <div class="slc-label">Case Study</div>
              <div class="slc-title">Managing Hallucination Risk</div>
              <div class="slc-desc">Guardrails and validation patterns for safety-critical AI outputs.</div>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:2rem 0;">
          <a href="/contact" class="study-link-card" style="flex:1; min-width:250px;">
            <div class="slc-label">Implementing this?</div>
            <div class="slc-title">Download Pilot Checklist →</div>
            <div class="slc-desc">Step-by-step guide to deploying a Review agent in your PV environment.</div>
          </a>
          <a href="/contact" class="study-link-card" style="flex:1; min-width:250px;">
            <div class="slc-label">Evaluating vendors?</div>
            <div class="slc-title">Get the RFP Template →</div>
            <div class="slc-desc">Pre-built questions for evaluating AI-powered review solutions.</div>
          </a>
        </div>
        
        <div class="feedback-bar">
          <p>Was this deep dive useful?</p>
          <button class="feedback-btn" onclick="this.classList.add('selected')">👍 Yes</button>
          <button class="feedback-btn" onclick="this.classList.add('selected')">👎 Needs work</button>
          <a href="/contact" style="font-size:0.75rem; color:rgba(241,236,224,0.5); margin-left:auto;">Found an error? Let us know →</a>
        </div>
        
        <div class="version-history">
          <h4>Version History</h4>
          <div class="version-entry">
            <span class="version-tag">v2.0</span>
            <span class="version-date">2025-06-02</span>
            <span>Added Under the Hood section, risk matrix, vendor landscape, sample demos, and citation-sourced KPIs.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="version-entry">
            <span class="version-tag">v1.0</span>
            <span class="version-date">2024-11-01</span>
            <span>Initial architecture and capabilities published.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <nav class="pipeline-nav">
          <a href="/agents/meddra-coding">
            <div>
              <span class="pn-label">← Previous Agent</span>
              <span class="pn-name">MedDRA Coding Agent</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/agents/aggregate-reporting" style="text-align:right">
            <div>
              <span class="pn-label">Next Agent →</span>
